-- title:
--   An away-from-v unit of reduced norm r
-- statement:
--   Fix natural numbers $r$, $\bar r$, $N$ with $r$ and $\bar r$ prime, $N \neq 0$, $\bar r \neq r$ and $r \nmid N$, and rationals $a_1, b_1$ such that the quaternion algebra $H = \mathbb{H}[\mathbb{Q}, a_1, b_1]$ satisfies `IsDefiniteRamifiedExactlyAt` $\bar r$, i.e. $a_1 < 0$, $b_1 < 0$, and for every height-one prime $v$ of $\mathcal{O}_{\mathbb{Q}}$ the completed algebra $H \otimes_{\mathbb{Q}} \mathbb{Q}_v$ has every nonzero element invertible exactly when $\bar r$ lies in the ideal of $v$. Let $\Lambda_1, R_1$ be $\mathbb{Z}$-submodules of $H$ with: $\Lambda_1$ an order (containing $1$, closed under multiplication, spanning $H$ over $\mathbb{Q}$, finitely generated) that is maximal among orders containing it; $R_1$ an Eichler order of level $N$, that is, an intersection $\Lambda' \cap \Lambda''$ of two maximal orders whose relative index in $\Lambda'$ as additive subgroups is $N$; and $R_1 \le \Lambda_1$. Let $v$ be a height-one prime of $\mathcal{O}_{\mathbb{Q}}$ whose ideal contains $r$. Then there exists a unit $w$ of $H$ lying in `awayUnits` $R_1\, v$ — so that for every height-one prime $u \neq v$ the image of $w$ in the units of $H \otimes_{\mathbb{Q}} \mathbb{Q}_u$ lies in the subgroup generated by those units $x$ of $H \otimes_{\mathbb{Q}} \mathbb{Q}_u$ with both $x$ and $x^{-1}$ in the local box of $R_1$ at $u$ — and with reduced norm $\mathrm{nrd}(w) = r$, where $\mathrm{nrd}(x) = x_{\mathrm{re}}^2 - a_1 x_{i}^2 - b_1 x_{j}^2 + a_1 b_1 x_{k}^2$.
--
--   This is the Hasse–Schilling norm theorem for the definite algebra $H$ (every positive rational, in particular $r$, is a reduced norm) combined with strong approximation for the norm-one group away from the place $v$ above $r$, where $H$ is split; the conclusion produces a global quaternion unit integral and invertible at all places other than $v$ whose reduced norm has odd valuation at $v$. It is used in the Čerednik–Drinfeld uniformisation arguments for quaternionic modular curves, where such an element realigns the coefficient leg in the surjectivity statements for level structures.
